# Developer Knowledge Profile

Initial profile for the decision maker (Senior .NET backend). Levels evolve from **observed** interactions — not from the “Senior .NET” title alone.

## Levels

| Level | Meaning | Explain | Capitalize |
|---|---|---|---|
| **KNOWN** | Solid mastery | No systematic pedagogy | No |
| **LEARNING** | Actively learning | Important concepts yes | Possible if criteria met |
| **UNKNOWN** | Not yet assessed | Short first pass; observe | Never auto-create Notion |

## Initial map

### KNOWN

C#, .NET, ASP.NET Core, EF Core, PostgreSQL / SQL, DDD, software architecture, backend APIs, backend testing, common backend patterns.

### LEARNING

- TypeScript — beginner
- JavaScript — intermediate / learning
- React — beginner
- CSS / frontend UI — general knowledge, not expertise
- Angular — beginner (secondary vs React for Play’Up 11.3+)

### UNKNOWN

Anything not listed. Short intro on first encounter; watch questions, corrections, and autonomous implementations.

## Evolution

- Evidence of mastery (correct usage, precise corrections, independent design) → stop treating as new; may move toward KNOWN.
- Persistent confusion → keep explaining at LEARNING depth.
- Propose updating Notion Technologies **Niveau de maîtrise** only when the shift is clear — do not sync on every message.

Notion mapping (when syncing mastery): KNOWN ≈ `⭐ Maîtrisé` / `🟢 Utilisé régulièrement`; LEARNING ≈ `🟡 En apprentissage`; UNKNOWN ≈ `🔵 À découvrir`.
